/target
# Same class as `/target`: alternate build directories. `.buildtarget` is used
# when the `target` symlink points at a mount that is temporarily unavailable
# (see the WSL storage incident), and `target.bak` is a snapshot of a previous
# one. Neither is part of the project, and both are large.
/.buildtarget
/target.bak
/build
/.pir

# Local scratch from debugging sessions (not part of the project).
# Kept out of `git status` so real changes stand out; nothing here is
# referenced by the build or tests.
/.resume/
/.tmp/
/www/
/canary
/canary.txt
/null
/mypy.py
/thinkblanks.py
/raven.log*
/raven.stderr*
/TODO.txt

# Command Code's own agent state (plans, taste, settings). Not part of pir's
# source tree; ignoring it keeps `git status` about real changes and lets the
# auto-commit tool stage cleanly.
/.commandcode/
